(7482514, 1189610, 139239, '<td valign="top">I think it''s a spot-on photo which is nicely done. Great colors and perspective.</td>', 'I think it''s a spot-on photo which is nicely done. Great colors and perspective.', '2016-11-14 11:13:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482515, 1190220, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that does not meet the challenge<br/> <br/>Youre right Eugene, I recognised that amazing lens immediately! Whilst I do like your image, I have to agree with your commenters, in the strict interpretation of the challenge brief it is more abstract than impressionism. As an abstract it is excellent a truly unique representation of fireworks that I doubt any viewer was able to figure out without your engaging explanation. I very much like your creative approach in using the amazing array of lenses in bold experimental ways that enable you to create some very original images, keep up the good work.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that does not meet the challenge Youre right Eugene, I recognised that amazing lens immediately! Whilst I do like your image, I have to agree with your commenters, in the strict interpretation of the challenge brief it is more abstract than impressionism. As an abstract it is excellent a truly unique representation of fireworks that I doubt any viewer was able to figure out without your engaging explanation. I very much like your creative approach in using the amazing array of lenses in bold experimental ways that enable you to create some very original images, keep up the good work.', '2016-11-14 11:53:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482516, 1190062, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>You have some lovely bright colours for your flowers which work well against the interesting background. Whilst I can see why you have used this filter to fulfil the challenge brief I am no fan of these filters at all so Im not really in a position to give you an unbiased opinion. I see the title is indeed most accurate hope you are having or have had an enjoyable time in France Janine.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge You have some lovely bright colours for your flowers which work well against the interesting background. Whilst I can see why you have used this filter to fulfil the challenge brief I am no fan of these filters at all so Im not really in a position to give you an unbiased opinion. I see the title is indeed most accurate hope you are having or have had an enjoyable time in France Janine.', '2016-11-14 11:59:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482518, 1189895, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>I like your composition and the colours within it. Whilst I can see why you have used this filter to fulfil the challenge brief I am no fan of these filters at all so Im not really in a position to give you an unbiased opinion. I much prefer to see impressionism done in-camera, a couple of options to achieve this would be either to use a slow shutter speed with motion blur or complete lack of focus to produce a soft dreamy effect.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge I like your composition and the colours within it. Whilst I can see why you have used this filter to fulfil the challenge brief I am no fan of these filters at all so Im not really in a position to give you an unbiased opinion. I much prefer to see impressionism done in-camera, a couple of options to achieve this would be either to use a slow shutter speed with motion blur or complete lack of focus to produce a soft dreamy effect.', '2016-11-14 12:03:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482519, 1190233, 182284, '<td valign="top">I surely thought this photo would have done much better. I gave a 10 on this.</td>', 'I surely thought this photo would have done much better. I gave a 10 on this.', '2016-11-14 12:03:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482520, 1190233, 182284, '<td valign="top">My internet is acting weird. Sorry double post.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-11-14 12:05:49.</i></td>', 'My internet is acting weird. Sorry double post.', '2016-11-14 12:04:17.000000', '2016-11-14 12:05:49.000000', 0),
(7482521, 1189744, 182284, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot and I do like the filter you used. It''s perfect.</td>', 'Beautiful shot and I do like the filter you used. It''s perfect.', '2016-11-14 12:10:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482525, 1190239, 98565, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the HM - i like how you achieved the impressionistic feel without using a PS filter!<br/>But overall this picture is a little bit too dull for my taste and I wonder if I''d like it even more with adding contrast and/or adjusting levels</td>', 'Congrats on the HM - i like how you achieved the impressionistic feel without using a PS filter!But overall this picture is a little bit too dull for my taste and I wonder if I''d like it even more with adding contrast and/or adjusting levels', '2016-11-14 13:44:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482526, 1190059, 86447, '<td valign="top">Nicely done, Diane!</td>', 'Nicely done, Diane!', '2016-11-14 13:48:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482527, 1190204, 86447, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your HM!</td>', 'Congratulations on your HM!', '2016-11-14 13:52:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482528, 1190239, 86447, '<td valign="top">Interesting effect... and no PS!    Congrats on your HM!<br/></td>', 'Interesting effect... and no PS!    Congrats on your HM!', '2016-11-14 13:53:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482534, 1190204, 182284, '<td valign="top">Beautiful, I gave a 10. Great job.</td>', 'Beautiful, I gave a 10. Great job.', '2016-11-14 14:37:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482535, 1190059, 182284, '<td valign="top">Beautiful and congrats. I gave an 8.</td>', 'Beautiful and congrats. I gave an 8.', '2016-11-14 14:38:53.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(7482536, 1190226, 182284, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! Great job. I''m hoping through your photos via osmosis I will become more creative. LOL<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-11-17 00:09:32.</i></td>', 'Congratulations! Great job. I''m hoping through your photos via osmosis I will become more creative. LOL', '2016-11-14 14:39:41.000000', '2016-11-17 00:09:32.000000', 0),
(7482537, 1190040, 182284, '<td valign="top">Congratulations. lovely masterpiece.</td>', 'Congratulations. lovely masterpiece.', '2016-11-14 14:40:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482538, 1190204, 142425, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by riot:</b></div><hr/><i> Relies on a photoshop effect to produce the majority of its value in meeting the challenge: 4. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Also relies on a camera, a computer, the Internet. Just a 2 then.</td>', 'Originally posted by riot: Relies on a photoshop effect to produce the majority of its value in meeting the challenge: 4.   Also relies on a camera, a computer, the Internet. Just a 2 then.', '2016-11-14 14:51:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482539, 1190276, 138630, '<td valign="top">I love the dancing light and colors behind the chorus line.  I gave it a 6 and almost bumped it, but for me the foreground flower heads were too dark and heavy and static - they weighed it down where I wanted them to lift it up - or at least live up to the airiness and movement of the background.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-11-14 15:57:00.</i></td>', 'I love the dancing light and colors behind the chorus line.  I gave it a 6 and almost bumped it, but for me the foreground flower heads were too dark and heavy and static - they weighed it down where I wanted them to lift it up - or at least live up to the airiness and movement of the background.', '2016-11-14 15:54:43.000000', '2016-11-14 15:57:00.000000', 0),
(7482545, 1190096, 86447, '<td valign="top">"Never liked these types of topics but they are quitechallenging. "<br/> <br/>I''ll agree to that!    *sigh*   Not much fun for me either.<br/> <br/>I like your composition, but I think the cup is a negative distraction.</td>', '"Never liked these types of topics but they are quitechallenging. " I''ll agree to that!    *sigh*   Not much fun for me either. I like your composition, but I think the cup is a negative distraction.', '2016-11-14 17:48:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482563, 1190228, 123833, '<td valign="top">Absolutely fantastic photo, Mary Ann. Highly under-appreciated. The obsession with meeting the challenge at DPC sometimes just goes too far and great work receives much too low scores. Pity that there is no longer emphasis on quality as in this very fine example.</td>', 'Absolutely fantastic photo, Mary Ann. Highly under-appreciated. The obsession with meeting the challenge at DPC sometimes just goes too far and great work receives much too low scores. Pity that there is no longer emphasis on quality as in this very fine example.', '2016-11-14 22:33:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482569, 1190217, 100831, '<td valign="top">This was a 7 from me... And it''s growing. The colors make it shine.</td>', 'This was a 7 from me... And it''s growing. The colors make it shine.', '2016-11-14 23:19:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482575, 1190185, 117474, '<td valign="top">knew this had to be you. actually this feels like an image that would be great with a grungy feeling. (though I tend to think about that with most images these days! :D)</td>', 'knew this had to be you. actually this feels like an image that would be great with a grungy feeling. (though I tend to think about that with most images these days! :D)', '2016-11-14 23:36:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482578, 1190245, 117474, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by riot:</b></div><hr/><i> Relies on a photoshop filter to produce its entire value in meeting the challenge: 1. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>it''s funny you know. i don''t quite understand why reliance on photoshop filters is such a crime as to deserve a 1, in particular since this image is about more than the trivial application of a single filter. the darks, and lights, and transitions therein and between are quite lovely. for me this image unquestionably had the best application of this filter in the challenge. it''s subtle enough so you don''t notice it at a distance, but as you inspect the details you begin to see fractal-like veins emerging from the shrubbery, and the filter you applied enhances this. combined with the darks, slight softness, and hidden details... lovely. <br/> <br/>it seems so obvious to me that this image isn''t a trivial application of a filter, so i''m a bit annoyed about the comment you received. keep it up! i gave a 9 for this.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-11-14 23:52:41.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by riot: Relies on a photoshop filter to produce its entire value in meeting the challenge: 1.  it''s funny you know. i don''t quite understand why reliance on photoshop filters is such a crime as to deserve a 1, in particular since this image is about more than the trivial application of a single filter. the darks, and lights, and transitions therein and between are quite lovely. for me this image unquestionably had the best application of this filter in the challenge. it''s subtle enough so you don''t notice it at a distance, but as you inspect the details you begin to see fractal-like veins emerging from the shrubbery, and the filter you applied enhances this. combined with the darks, slight softness, and hidden details... lovely.  it seems so obvious to me that this image isn''t a trivial application of a filter, so i''m a bit annoyed about the comment you received. keep it up! i gave a 9 for this.', '2016-11-14 23:43:34.000000', '2016-11-14 23:52:41.000000', 0),
(7482589, 1190204, 97225, '<td valign="top">Congrats Margaret, nice work.</td>', 'Congrats Margaret, nice work.', '2016-11-15 00:09:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482641, 1190040, 135744, '<td valign="top">Congrats! I wonder if this is the first drone blue ribbon. Either way it is a superb image.</td>', 'Congrats! I wonder if this is the first drone blue ribbon. Either way it is a superb image.', '2016-11-15 04:23:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482660, 1190002, 140305, '<td valign="top">This got high marks from me. I thought it fit the challenge perfectly and was beautiful to boot! I thought this would finish higher.</td>', 'This got high marks from me. I thought it fit the challenge perfectly and was beautiful to boot! I thought this would finish higher.', '2016-11-15 10:13:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482667, 1190187, 138630, '<td valign="top">This was actually my top pick - I am your only 10 and yours was my only 10 :)  I found the scene perfect - my immediate thought was Berthe Morisot but others came to mind, too.  I liked that it wasn''t a re-creation of any that I knew but evoked them immediately, in light and tones as well as subject.  And of course I didn''t mind the art texture that seemed to me absolutely appropriate for the challenge.</td>', 'This was actually my top pick - I am your only 10 and yours was my only 10 :)  I found the scene perfect - my immediate thought was Berthe Morisot but others came to mind, too.  I liked that it wasn''t a re-creation of any that I knew but evoked them immediately, in light and tones as well as subject.  And of course I didn''t mind the art texture that seemed to me absolutely appropriate for the challenge.', '2016-11-15 11:20:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482672, 1190228, 138630, '<td valign="top">This was second highest pick and a 9, Mary Ann.  <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=124815" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">mariuca</a>''s is a good comment, I think, in that the Impressionists didn''t do that many still lifes (maybe pre-Impressionism which Monet kind of is to me) and when they did, they were much sparer.  But I will diverge from her on the use of the filter which I find imminently suitable for this lavish display - the heavy drape, the ruffly blossoms, the nest tucked in among the pears, even the vase.  I found it wonderfully successful.</td>', 'This was second highest pick and a 9, Mary Ann.   mariuca''s is a good comment, I think, in that the Impressionists didn''t do that many still lifes (maybe pre-Impressionism which Monet kind of is to me) and when they did, they were much sparer.  But I will diverge from her on the use of the filter which I find imminently suitable for this lavish display - the heavy drape, the ruffly blossoms, the nest tucked in among the pears, even the vase.  I found it wonderfully successful.', '2016-11-15 11:30:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482765, 1190143, 16148, '<td valign="top">Erasing tire tracks.  A clean canvas by morning.</td>', 'Erasing tire tracks.  A clean canvas by morning.', '2016-11-15 21:27:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482776, 1190148, 182284, '<td valign="top">Beautiful place. Reminds me of one of my favorite places. I gave you a 10 on this one.</td>', 'Beautiful place. Reminds me of one of my favorite places. I gave you a 10 on this one.', '2016-11-15 22:02:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482777, 1190148, 182284, '<td valign="top">Sorry double post.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-11-15 22:04:03.</i></td>', 'Sorry double post.', '2016-11-15 22:02:46.000000', '2016-11-15 22:04:03.000000', 0),
(7482790, 1190228, 86447, '<td valign="top">I would vote this a ten... in an different challenge topic.  You''re amazing at this thing!   <br/> <br/>This is stunningly gorgeous, Mary Ann!<br/></td>', 'I would vote this a ten... in an different challenge topic.  You''re amazing at this thing!    This is stunningly gorgeous, Mary Ann!', '2016-11-15 23:13:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482820, 1190250, 68504, '<td valign="top">but of course we like a saturday night bar dog. whatever mind we''re in.</td>', 'but of course we like a saturday night bar dog. whatever mind we''re in.', '2016-11-16 01:32:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7482855, 1190212, 117474, '<td valign="top">:)</td>', ':)', '2016-11-16 15:30:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7483037, 1190002, 114285, '<td valign="top">This was a great shot, another one I should''ve bumped! Filter you used was spot on!</td>', 'This was a great shot, another one I should''ve bumped! Filter you used was spot on!', '2016-11-17 22:27:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7483191, 1190203, 115814, '<td valign="top">This is really lovely and very appropriately impressionistic. Its has the characteristics of both a photo that has been processed with filter AND the look of a painting that''s been photographed.</td>', 'This is really lovely and very appropriately impressionistic. Its has the characteristics of both a photo that has been processed with filter AND the look of a painting that''s been photographed.', '2016-11-19 01:42:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(7483210, 1190245, 50695, '<td valign="top">I would have like a more subtle or blended application of the filter, but this still merited a 6 from me</td>', 'I would have like a more subtle or blended application of the filter, but this still merited a 6 from me', '2016-11-19 11:29:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7483233, 1190245, 14476, '<td valign="top">I gave this an eight because it is handsome and meets the challenge.<br/>If you used one or more filters, you used them intelligently and with meaning.<br/></td>', 'I gave this an eight because it is handsome and meets the challenge.If you used one or more filters, you used them intelligently and with meaning.', '2016-11-19 18:43:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7483945, 1190059, 115814, '<td valign="top">Stopped by your this photo after seeing your name on the "Post Challenge Comments Volunteers" thread. I scored this a 7 and enjoyed your take on the challenge. I think this a great example of filters adding interest to a photo. The effect here distils the image to its colorful essence. As a straight photo, it would have been just another fall color cliche.<br/></td>', 'Stopped by your this photo after seeing your name on the "Post Challenge Comments Volunteers" thread. I scored this a 7 and enjoyed your take on the challenge. I think this a great example of filters adding interest to a photo. The effect here distils the image to its colorful essence. As a straight photo, it would have been just another fall color cliche.', '2016-11-23 19:52:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(7484842, 1190228, 37858, '<td valign="top">This is stunning!  Beautiful image in every way.</td>', 'This is stunning!  Beautiful image in every way.', '2016-11-28 15:36:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(7485018, 1190217, 117474, '<td valign="top">this is very cool indeed! :)</td>', 'this is very cool indeed! :)', '2016-11-29 17:06:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(7490879, 1189869, 24744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mitalapo:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by riot:</b></div><hr/><i> Relies on a photoshop filter to produce the majority of its value in meeting the challenge: 2. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>broken preconceptions are gold.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>This relies on the "digital zoom" feature of an iphone, which acts by blowing up the original image and tiling in new pixels in a bilateral blur, a "smart blur" effect; this is absolutely no different than a photoshop filter, the only change is that it''s done by your phone''s software instead of by photoshop.  I''m sorry if this offends you, but I stand entirely by my comment - this photograph is nothing at all without reliance on an entirely digital effect.</td>', 'Originally posted by mitalapo: Originally posted by riot: Relies on a photoshop filter to produce the majority of its value in meeting the challenge: 2.  broken preconceptions are gold. This relies on the "digital zoom" feature of an iphone, which acts by blowing up the original image and tiling in new pixels in a bilateral blur, a "smart blur" effect; this is absolutely no different than a photoshop filter, the only change is that it''s done by your phone''s software instead of by photoshop.  I''m sorry if this offends you, but I stand entirely by my comment - this photograph is nothing at all without reliance on an entirely digital effect.', '2017-01-07 10:13:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7490892, 1189869, 53814, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by riot:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m sorry if this offends you, but I stand entirely by my comment - this photograph is nothing at all without reliance on an entirely digital effect. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It is your obnoxious presentation, not your comment, that is offensive.  A good photographer understands the technical details. An excellent photographer has forgotten them. A soul-less photographer judges the worth of a photo by them.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2017-01-07 13:07:47.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by riot: I''m sorry if this offends you, but I stand entirely by my comment - this photograph is nothing at all without reliance on an entirely digital effect.   It is your obnoxious presentation, not your comment, that is offensive.  A good photographer understands the technical details. An excellent photographer has forgotten them. A soul-less photographer judges the worth of a photo by them.', '2017-01-07 12:35:55.000000', '2017-01-07 13:07:47.000000', 0),
(7491714, 1189869, 24744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pointandshoot:</b></div><hr/><i>It is your obnoxious presentation, not your comment, that is offensive.  A good photographer understands the technical details. An excellent photographer has forgotten them. A soul-less photographer judges the worth of a photo by them. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>These irrelevant generalisations don''t suffice to hide the utter nonsense of your primary statement.<br/> <br/>None of what I said has been in any way "obnoxious".  After taking the trouble to vote on a contest (on a site that has rapidly diminsihing voter numbers), I have subsequently taken the trouble to clearly and politely comment, explaining my vote - something that, as I''m sure you''re aware, increasingly few participants of the site do these days.  Receiving this kind of information is something that I personally value very highly on my own work, from other voters.  I have subsequently returned to the discussion to answer some snide remarks, and explain precisely why what I said was appropriate, technically correct, and why I stand behind it - again, clearly and politely.<br/> <br/>As for the discussion on why I chose to rate images low in this contest that relied entirely on digital effects, that was well covered in the forum post that 2mccs also participated in at the time of the contest, and doesn''t need to be rehashed here.<br/> <br/>The fact is it''s thin skinned critiqueophobes such as yourself who have driven the site into its current sorry state, where everyone is terrified of explaining their vote, or sharing the faults they found in the photograph with its creator - for fear of having some sanctimonious commenter attack them in the comments with some semi-ad-hominem generalisation rubbish, as you''ve done, about what a "soul-less photographer" does, because they have found fault in yours or someone else''s image.  The fact also is that most photographers come to this site to learn and improve their skills, and attitudes such as yours are directly interfering with them receiving the very critique they need.<br/> <br/>I don''t intend to bow to that sort of rubbish from you and others like you, but I do intend to call it out when I see it, because it''s important that everyone here who complains about the current commentless state of the site is aware - it''s exactly people like you who have brought it to this state.</td>', 'Originally posted by pointandshoot:It is your obnoxious presentation, not your comment, that is offensive.  A good photographer understands the technical details. An excellent photographer has forgotten them. A soul-less photographer judges the worth of a photo by them.  These irrelevant generalisations don''t suffice to hide the utter nonsense of your primary statement. None of what I said has been in any way "obnoxious".  After taking the trouble to vote on a contest (on a site that has rapidly diminsihing voter numbers), I have subsequently taken the trouble to clearly and politely comment, explaining my vote - something that, as I''m sure you''re aware, increasingly few participants of the site do these days.  Receiving this kind of information is something that I personally value very highly on my own work, from other voters.  I have subsequently returned to the discussion to answer some snide remarks, and explain precisely why what I said was appropriate, technically correct, and why I stand behind it - again, clearly and politely. As for the discussion on why I chose to rate images low in this contest that relied entirely on digital effects, that was well covered in the forum post that 2mccs also participated in at the time of the contest, and doesn''t need to be rehashed here. The fact is it''s thin skinned critiqueophobes such as yourself who have driven the site into its current sorry state, where everyone is terrified of explaining their vote, or sharing the faults they found in the photograph with its creator - for fear of having some sanctimonious commenter attack them in the comments with some semi-ad-hominem generalisation rubbish, as you''ve done, about what a "soul-less photographer" does, because they have found fault in yours or someone else''s image.  The fact also is that most photographers come to this site to learn and improve their skills, and attitudes such as yours are directly interfering with them receiving the very critique they need. I don''t intend to bow to that sort of rubbish from you and others like you, but I do intend to call it out when I see it, because it''s important that everyone here who complains about the current commentless state of the site is aware - it''s exactly people like you who have brought it to this state.', '2017-01-11 11:33:49.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
